      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-09T00:20:33Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): place a setup relative to another; transform between setups\n\nOne rigid transform per setup: the #326 part alignment. The transform\nfrom setup A to setup B is derived from the two alignments\n(setup_relative::transform_between, T = A_B * A_A^-1), refusing a\nmissing setup, a non-setup and a non-rigid stored alignment by name.\n\nA setup may now be placed relative to another (SetupDef::relative_to,\nSetSetupRelative::link / unlink): \"flip over X / turn 90 about Z / typed\nangles from <setup>\" resolves into the setup's part alignment through\nAlignPartToSetup, so the stock follows as in #326. A later change of the\nparent's alignment re-places every linked setup (transitively) in the\nsame undo unit, keeping its transform to the parent, or refuses the\nwhole change naming the setup that cannot follow. Self links and loops\nare refused; DeleteSetup refuses a parent. Datum transfer does not link\n(a clone, not an alias); nothing is read from the work offset.\n\nProject v56: SetupDto::relative_to (absent = not linked); a link to no\nsetup or a loop of links is a corrupt file. The setup page offers\n\"Relative to previous setup\". Decisions: docs/decisions/316-setup-transform.md.\n\nFixes #316\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
